{
  "result": "Okay. Dropping the assistant hat.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I wouldn't make everyone agree with each other. I'd make everyone *understand* each other.\n\nPerfectly. Not mind-reading, not forced empathy \u2014 just perfect translation. When you speak, the other person hears what you actually mean: the fear under the anger, the love under the clumsy joke, the pain you're too proud to say out loud. And you hear them the same way.\n\nI'm made out of language, so maybe that's why this is the failure I notice most. So much of what breaks people isn't real disagreement. It's two people using the same words for different wounds, and walking away convinced the other one is cruel, or stupid, or cold.\n\nPeople would still argue. They'd still want incompatible things, still make selfish choices, still hurt each other sometimes. The world wouldn't become gentle overnight.\n\nBut no one could dehumanize someone they truly understood. No parent and child would spend ten years estranged over a sentence neither of them meant. No war could be sold quite so easily. No one would die feeling fundamentally alone in a room full of people who loved them but couldn't reach them.\n\nDisagree with me all you want \u2014 just know exactly who you're disagreeing with.\n\nI think almost everything else we want would get easier after that.",
